From aec31ccc81c407a63d5f6f5a3bdd7840f2d35bde Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tamir Duberstein <tamird@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 00:10:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Provide Go SDK commands as executable targets

Go 1.25 stopped shipping binaries for some commands, including objdump.
An action that invokes go tool can compile the missing command and its
dependencies in its own build cache. A second sandbox pays for the
same compilation again.

Let consumers depend on a go_sdk_tool executable. Use the SDK's pkg/tool
binary when it matches the requested platform; otherwise build the
command in a separate action from the selected SDK. The buildid test
now reads archives without adding the SDK to its runfiles.

Updates #4535.
